plan
meta:
  id: domain-centric-applications
  title: Domain-centric applications inside one Site
  project: meowbox
  status: approved-for-implementation-planning
  date: 2026-07-30
  release_model: one release, one update run, mandatory automatic preflight

goal:
  summary: >
    Allow one Site to host multiple independently managed applications by making
    every main SiteDomain the owner of exactly one preset/application.
  outcomes:
    - create one Site with one or several domain/application pairs
    - add another managed domain/application to an existing Site
    - manage MODX, PHP, files, databases, logs, deploy and admin login per domain
    - preserve aliases, SSL and current per-domain Nginx configuration
    - migrate every supported existing installation in one release

fixed_decisions:
  D01:
    rule: SiteDomain is the application boundary
    detail: >
      No SiteApplication or ApplicationEndpoint table. A main SiteDomain row
      contains its domain routing settings and its one application preset.
  D02:
    rule: one main domain equals one application
    detail: Aliases route to that same application and never become applications.
  D03:
    rule: UI is domain-centric
    detail: >
      Domain selector in Site header selects both domain and application. There
      is no second application selector.
  D04:
    rule: use only existing presets
    values: [MODX_REVO, MODX_3, CUSTOM]
  D05:
    rule: every domain uses its own explicit filesRelPath
    detail: >
      No apps/<slug>/www layout and no implicit new directory hierarchy.
  D06:
    rule: no manual application discovery or adoption
  D07:
    rule: no UNMANAGED preset
    detail: Existing secondary domains migrate to CUSTOM.
  D08:
    rule: no bulk MODX update action
    detail: MODX update is available only for the selected domain.
  D09:
    rule: appPort stays internal
    detail: >
      Do not expose appPort in generic Site or Domain creation forms. Preserve
      existing non-null values and current Node/custom-Nginx behavior.
  D10:
    rule: preserve current per-domain Nginx layout
    detail: >
      Keep one Site server-block file with existing per-SiteDomain layered
      chunks. Change only domain payloads and generated PHP upstreams.
  D11:
    rule: one PHP-FPM pool and socket per PHP-enabled domain
    detail: >
      Do not create a systemd service per domain. One phpX.Y-fpm service hosts
      every pool that uses that PHP version.
  D12:
    rule: migration is one-shot
    detail: >
      Schema, data, API, agent, Web UI and system configuration switch in one
      release and one update run. No user-visible compatibility phase.
  D13:
    rule: update must prove migration before mutating production
    detail: >
      Automatic preflight runs the real DB migration against a SQLite clone and
      renders all system configs into a staging tree before maintenance mode.
  D14:
    rule: preserve legacy runtime paths where changing them is unnecessary
    detail: >
      Existing primary application keeps its filesRelPath, database contents,
      encrypted credentials, MODX paths, PHP version and compatible pool key.

non_goals:
  - multiple applications behind one main domain or path-based routing
  - one application shared by several main SiteDomain rows
  - automatic recognition of manually installed CMS applications
  - converting arbitrary existing custom content into a managed MODX preset
  - container-level isolation between applications inside one Site
  - bulk update of all MODX applications
  - a separate application navigation hierarchy
  - automatic mutation of MODX content when a domain is renamed
  - exposing reverse-proxy appPort in generic forms
  - moving existing application files into a new directory layout

domain_model:
  Site:
    responsibility:
      - shared Linux user and home/root directory
      - SSH access and encrypted SSH credential
      - aggregate ownership, quota and disk usage
      - whole-Site start/stop/delete lifecycle
      - whole-Site backups, schedules, services and host migration
      - container-level operational status and error
    retained_fields:
      - id
      - name
      - displayName
      - rootPath
      - nginxConfigPath
      - systemUser
      - sshPasswordEnc
      - userId
      - status
      - errorMessage
      - metadata
      - createdAt
      - updatedAt
    removed_application_fields:
      - domain
      - aliases
      - type
      - phpVersion
      - phpEnabled
      - phpPoolCustom
      - dbEnabled
      - filesRelPath
      - appPort
      - gitRepository
      - deployBranch
      - envVars
      - cmsAdminUser
      - cmsAdminPasswordEnc
      - managerPath
      - connectorsPath
      - cmsTablePrefix
      - modxVersion

  SiteDomain:
    responsibility:
      - canonical hostname and aliases
      - exactly one preset/application
      - application root and runtime settings
      - application lifecycle status
      - domain Nginx, SSL and HTTP behavior
      - selected-domain management context
    routing_fields:
      - id
      - siteId
      - domain
      - aliases
      - isPrimary
      - position
      - httpsRedirect
      - nginxSecurityProfile
      - nginxRateLimit
      - nginxCountryRules
      - nginxCustomConfig
      - existing layered Nginx settings
      - appPort
    application_fields:
      preset:
        type: existing SiteType enum
        required: true
        values: [MODX_REVO, MODX_3, CUSTOM]
      appStatus:
        type: DomainApplicationStatus
        required: true
        values: [PROVISIONING, RUNNING, DEPLOYING, UPDATING, ERROR]
      appErrorMessage:
        type: nullable string
      filesRelPath:
        type: string
        required: true
        rule: normalized relative path resolved strictly inside Site.rootPath
      phpVersion:
        type: nullable supported PHP version
      phpPoolCustom:
        type: nullable text
      runtimeKey:
        type: immutable unique short string
        purpose: stable PHP pool, socket, log and operation artifact key
      gitRepository:
        type: nullable string
      deployBranch:
        type: nullable string
      envVars:
        type: structured JSON
      cmsAdminUser:
        type: nullable string
      cmsAdminPasswordEnc:
        type: nullable encrypted string
      managerPath:
        type: nullable string
      connectorsPath:
        type: nullable string
      cmsTablePrefix:
        type: nullable string
      modxVersion:
        type: nullable string
    derived_fields:
      phpEnabled: phpVersion != null
      canonicalUrl: protocol from SSL state plus domain
      applicationLabel: domain plus preset

  Database:
    changes:
      - add required siteDomainId ownership after migration
      - retain siteId for efficient whole-Site ownership and deletion checks
      - add purpose enum APP_PRIMARY or AUXILIARY
      - add relation and index by siteDomainId
    invariants:
      - database.siteId equals database.siteDomain.siteId
      - MODX domain has exactly one APP_PRIMARY MARIADB-compatible database
      - CUSTOM domain may have zero or one APP_PRIMARY and any auxiliaries
      - at most one APP_PRIMARY database per domain
    database_enforcement:
      - raw partial unique SQLite index for one APP_PRIMARY per siteDomainId
      - service transaction validates cross-relation siteId equality

  DeployLog:
    changes:
      - add required siteDomainId
      - move active deployment lock from Site to SiteDomain
      - keep siteId for aggregate history queries if currently required

  related_models:
    SslCertificate:
      decision: already domain-owned; retain siteId plus domainId
    Backup:
      decision: remain Site-owned and cover every domain root and Site database
    BackupConfig:
      decision: remain Site-owned
    SiteDiskSnapshot:
      decision: remain Site-owned
    CronJob:
      decision: remain Site-owned in this release
      rationale: same Linux user and no current app-level ownership contract
    SiteService:
      decision: remain Site-owned
    SiteQuickCommand:
      decision: remain Site-owned
    HealthCheckPing:
      decision: add nullable siteDomainId only where the check targets an app
    AuditLog:
      decision: include siteDomainId and operationId in domain operations

database_constraints:
  C01:
    invariant: every Site has at least one SiteDomain
    enforcement: service transaction plus migration verification
  C02:
    invariant: exactly one primary SiteDomain per Site
    enforcement:
      - partial unique index on SiteDomain(siteId) WHERE isPrimary = true
      - service blocks deletion of last/primary domain
      - primary domain has position zero
      - remaining positions are unique and contiguous after mutations
  C03:
    invariant: runtimeKey is globally unique and immutable
    enforcement: unique index and DTO omission from update APIs
  C04:
    invariant: filesRelPath resolves inside Site.rootPath
    enforcement: shared path validator used by API and agent
  C05:
    invariant: new managed applications do not share a root
    enforcement: service rejects duplicate resolved roots for new domains
    legacy_exception: >
      Existing duplicate roots are preserved and reported by migration. File
      deletion remains blocked while another domain references the same root.
  C06:
    invariant: aliases and canonical domains do not conflict globally
    enforcement: normalized hostname registry check inside one transaction
  C07:
    invariant: MODX application has PHP and APP_PRIMARY database
    enforcement: DTO validation, provisioning preflight and DB constraint checks
  C08:
    invariant: CUSTOM has no inferred runtime
    enforcement: only explicitly supplied existing settings are persisted
  C09:
    invariant: hostname comparisons are canonical
    enforcement:
      - trim whitespace
      - lowercase
      - remove one terminal DNS dot
      - convert IDN to validated ASCII form
      - validate label and total hostname lengths
      - reject unsupported wildcard placement

runtime_key:
  migrated_primary:
    value: current immutable Site.name
    reason: preserve current PHP pool/socket compatibility where possible
  new_domain:
    value: deterministic short key derived from full SiteDomain UUID
    format: d plus 20 lowercase hexadecimal SHA-256 characters
  validation:
    - unique in DB
    - safe character set
    - resulting Unix socket path stays below platform limit
    - collision aborts before configuration writes
  rename_behavior:
    - domain rename never changes runtimeKey
    - make-primary never changes runtimeKey

path_policy:
  input:
    - store relative path only
    - reject absolute paths
    - reject empty path, dot-dot traversal, NUL and control characters
    - normalize separators and redundant dot segments
    - resolve symlinks for destructive operations
  new_site:
    - primary domain keeps current default directory convention
    - additional rows require an explicit directory field
  add_domain:
    - directory is required in the same form as domain and preset
    - MODX target must be absent or empty before installation
    - CUSTOM may use an existing directory without type discovery
  destructive_actions:
    - compare canonical real paths against Site.rootPath
    - refuse removal when another SiteDomain references same canonical path
    - never remove a pre-existing non-empty directory during failed provisioning

preset_contracts:
  MODX_REVO:
    required:
      - filesRelPath
      - supported phpVersion
      - APP_PRIMARY database
      - normalized managerPath
      - normalized connectorsPath
    managed_actions:
      - install
      - version check
      - update
      - doctor
      - setup directory cleanup
      - admin credential management
      - admin auto-login
      - permission normalization
  MODX_3:
    required: same as MODX_REVO with preset-specific compatibility validation
    managed_actions: same as MODX_REVO
  CUSTOM:
    required:
      - filesRelPath
    optional:
      - phpVersion
      - PHP pool overrides
      - databases
      - git/deploy settings
      - env vars
      - Node.js configuration through existing Node.js management
    forbidden:
      - inferred CMS type
      - inferred MODX credentials
      - generic appPort form control

php_fpm:
  topology:
    - one pool per PHP-enabled SiteDomain
    - one socket per pool
    - one shared phpX.Y-fpm systemd service per PHP version
    - no per-domain systemd service
  generated_pool:
    identity: runtimeKey
    user: Site.systemUser
    group: Site.systemUser
    root: resolved SiteDomain.filesRelPath
    socket: stable runtimeKey-based path
    temp_and_session_defaults: preserve current Site-level paths
    overrides: SiteDomain.phpPoolCustom after existing sanitizer/validation
  isolation:
    provides:
      - independent PHP version
      - independent process limits and pool configuration
      - independent socket and PHP error log
      - independent failure and reload targeting at config level
    does_not_provide:
      - Linux-user isolation
      - filesystem isolation between applications in one Site
    security_note: >
      Applications share one Linux user by design. A customer requiring tenant
      isolation must use separate Sites.
  compatibility:
    - migrated primary keeps compatible pool/runtime key
    - do not move application files
    - preserve current open_basedir breadth for migrated applications
    - keep current shared Site temp/session defaults unless explicitly overridden
    - every domain receives an independent PHP error log
    - managed commands always call explicit phpX.Y binary
    - bare SSH php command follows primary domain PHP or system default
  resource_envelope:
    migration:
      - read effective current Site pool process-manager limits
      - identify every domain that currently receives managed PHP in Nginx
      - distribute current aggregate max_children across replacement pools
      - allocate at least one worker per pool and distribute remainder by position
      - preserve non-resource custom PHP directives on every replacement pool
      - abort when safe minimum exceeds current budget and host headroom is insufficient
    new_domain:
      - apply current platform default pool budget
      - check host memory/process/file-descriptor headroom before creation
    reporting:
      - show old aggregate worker ceiling
      - show every new pool ceiling
      - show projected worst-case memory before apply
  config_change:
    phases:
      - render pool into staging path
      - validate complete PHP-FPM config
      - write atomically with mode and owner
      - reload affected phpX.Y-fpm service
      - verify socket creation
      - render and validate Nginx against new socket
      - remove obsolete pool only after HTTP health check
    rollback:
      - restore old pool files
      - reload affected services
      - restore Nginx files
  php_version_change:
    - create and validate pool under new version first
    - switch selected domain Nginx only after new socket is live
    - health-check application
    - remove old-version pool after success
    - restore old pool and Nginx on failure

nginx:
  retained_layout:
    site_file: /etc/nginx/sites-available/<site>.conf
    domain_chunks: /etc/nginx/meowbox/<site>/<siteDomainId>/
    aliases: remain in selected main domain server_name
  changed_payload:
    - every rendered domain receives its own filesRelPath
    - every PHP domain receives its own phpVersion and pool socket
    - non-PHP domain omits managed 20-php.conf
    - appPort remains internal and only affects current proxy behavior
  unchanged:
    - per-domain SSL
    - per-domain redirect
    - per-domain security, rate limits and country rules
    - exact custom Nginx content unless sanitizer requires rejection
    - current server-block/chunk filesystem structure
  generation:
    - no new Nginx file hierarchy
    - regenerate only affected Site config during normal domain changes
    - migration renders every Site once because PHP socket ownership changes
    - serialize Nginx writes per Site
  validation:
    - render complete candidate tree
    - run nginx -t before replacing active files
    - atomic file replacement
    - reload, never restart, when validation passes
    - restore candidate snapshot on reload or HTTP probe failure

site_lifecycle:
  Site.status:
    meaning: global Site/container availability
    behavior:
      - whole-Site start/stop remains unchanged
      - a single domain update never sets Site to DEPLOYING or ERROR
      - Site ERROR is reserved for shared Linux/Nginx/container failures
  SiteDomain.appStatus:
    transitions:
      - PROVISIONING -> RUNNING
      - PROVISIONING -> ERROR
      - ERROR -> PROVISIONING on retry
      - RUNNING -> UPDATING
      - UPDATING -> RUNNING
      - UPDATING -> ERROR
      - RUNNING -> DEPLOYING
      - DEPLOYING -> RUNNING
      - DEPLOYING -> ERROR
    note: no per-domain start/stop control is added in this release
  aggregate_display:
    - global stopped state wins
    - otherwise show counts of running, provisioning/updating and failed domains
    - never hide a per-domain ERROR behind aggregate RUNNING

create_site:
  web_flow:
    shared_step:
      - display name
      - system name
      - owner
      - shared Site options
    domains_step:
      - repeatable domain/application rows
      - minimum one row
      - exactly one primary row
      - domain and aliases
      - explicit directory
      - preset
      - preset-specific PHP/database/MODX options
      - SSL request options
      - no appPort
    review_step:
      - show directories, presets, PHP versions and database names per domain
      - show conflicts before submission
  api:
    request: nested Site fields plus domains array
    transaction:
      - validate all hostnames and aliases globally
      - reserve Site and all SiteDomain rows
      - assign immutable runtime keys
      - reserve database records and names
      - create one parent operation with per-domain child steps
  provisioning_order:
    - create Linux user and Site root once
    - create every domain directory safely
    - provision databases
    - install each managed application with explicit PHP binary
    - generate all PHP pools
    - validate PHP services and sockets
    - render Nginx once with all domains
    - request SSL per domain after HTTP routes work
    - persist credentials and detected versions per domain
  failure_semantics:
    fatal_core_failure:
      - mark operation failed
      - roll back only artifacts proven to be created by this operation
      - never delete pre-existing paths
      - retain diagnostics with secrets redacted
    ssl_failure:
      - keep application RUNNING over HTTP
      - mark domain SSL state failed/pending separately

add_domain:
  web_flow:
    - one form combines domain, aliases, directory, preset and preset settings
    - reuses exact preset form components and validation from create Site
    - no separate application creation step
  api:
    - create SiteDomain plus dependent records transactionally
    - return operationId and per-step status
  concurrency:
    - Site mutation lock serializes Nginx/domain-list changes
    - SiteDomain operation lock serializes app provisioning/update/delete
  failure:
    - preserve existing Site and applications
    - keep failed SiteDomain in ERROR for retry and diagnostics
    - clean only newly created DB, pool, certificate request and empty directory

domain_selection_ui:
  location: Site detail page header
  behavior:
    - show selector only when more than one main SiteDomain exists
    - sort primary first, then position
    - option displays domain, preset badge and app status
    - aliases never appear as options
    - selected domain also selects its application
  url_state:
    format: ?domain=<siteDomainId>&tab=<tab>
    rules:
      - primary domain is default
      - invalid, unauthorized or deleted ID falls back to primary
      - every domain-specific link carries siteDomainId explicitly
      - selection survives refresh and can be shared
  tab_change:
    - preserve current tab when applicable
    - fall back to Overview when target domain lacks that capability
  no_hidden_context:
    - destructive dialogs repeat canonical domain and directory
    - API never infers selected domain from cookies or primary flag

web_information_architecture:
  domain_scoped:
    Overview:
      - preset, app status, root, runtime, version and domain URL
      - selected-domain actions only
    SSL:
      - selected SiteDomain certificate and aliases
    Nginx:
      - selected SiteDomain layered chunks and read-only full Site config link
    PHP:
      - visible when selected domain has phpVersion
      - selected pool/version/config/log only
    Databases:
      - list/create/manage databases owned by selected domain
      - identify APP_PRIMARY without exposing secrets
    Files:
      - root is selected SiteDomain.filesRelPath
      - breadcrumb cannot escape selected root
    Node.js:
      - processes and ecosystem files under selected domain root
      - preserve global PM2 name collision checks for shared Linux user
    Logs:
      - selected domain Nginx access/error log
      - selected domain PHP pool log when applicable
      - selected domain deploy/application operation logs
    MODX:
      - visible for MODX presets only
      - version/update, doctor, cleanup, credentials and admin login
    Deploy:
      - selected domain git/env/deploy state
  site_scoped:
    Domains:
      - all main domains and aliases
      - add, edit, order and make-primary
    DNS:
      - current Site/DNS-zone behavior with explicit domain labels
    Backups:
      - whole-Site backup covering all applications and databases
    Cron:
      - current shared Linux-user jobs
    Services:
      - current Site services
    SSH:
      - one shared Linux user
    Danger:
      - whole-Site destructive actions
  site_list:
    replace:
      - singular Site type badge
      - singular application version
    with:
      - domain count
      - preset counts or compact preset badges
      - aggregate application status
    filters:
      - preset filter matches any SiteDomain
      - error filter matches Site error or any domain app error

domain_management:
  rename:
    changes:
      - canonical hostname
      - Nginx server_name
      - SSL request/state
      - displayed admin URL
    preserves:
      - SiteDomain id
      - runtimeKey
      - filesRelPath
      - database ownership
      - PHP pool
      - MODX credentials and version
    restriction: do not silently rewrite CMS content or user configuration
  make_primary:
    changes:
      - atomic primary flag swap
      - atomic position reorder with replacement at position zero
      - default domain selection
      - Site-level canonical display URL
      - bare SSH php shim if primary PHP differs
    preserves:
      - every application and runtime artifact
      - directories, pools, databases, SSL and runtime keys
  delete:
    guards:
      - cannot delete last SiteDomain
      - primary must be changed first
      - reject while provisioning, updating, deploying or backing up
      - list shared paths and dependent databases before confirmation
    default:
      - remove Nginx route, SSL relation and domain PHP pool
      - preserve files and databases unless separately confirmed
    optional_destructive_flags:
      - delete application files
      - delete owned databases
    safety:
      - typed canonical domain confirmation
      - snapshot before destructive deletion
      - refuse file deletion for shared canonical path

api_contract:
  shared_guard:
    name: requireOwnedSiteDomain
    behavior:
      - load Site and SiteDomain in one ownership-scoped query
      - verify domain.siteId equals route siteId
      - verify current user/admin authorization
      - return normalized domain application context
  domain_routes:
    - GET /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/application
    - POST /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/application/retry
    - GET /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/php-pool-config
    - PUT /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/php-pool-config
    - POST /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/modx/update
    - GET /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/modx/doctor
    - POST /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/modx/cleanup-setup
    - POST /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/modx/admin-password
    - POST /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/modx/admin-login
    - GET /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/files
    - GET /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/logs
    - POST /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/deploy
    - GET /sites/:siteId/domains/:domainId/deploys
    - domain-scoped database and Node.js routes
  site_routes_retained:
    - whole-Site start/stop/delete
    - SSH credentials
    - whole-Site backups
    - Cron, Services and Site metadata
  compatibility:
    - Web UI and API switch together in same release
    - remove Site-level CMS/PHP/app endpoints after all internal callers migrate
    - do not silently redirect ambiguous old endpoints to primary domain
    - return explicit 410 or validation error for stale external clients
  validation:
    - DTOs accept IDs and declarative settings, never absolute runtime paths
    - agent receives server-derived normalized context
    - reject unsupported PHP/MODX combinations before side effects
    - cap aliases, env size, custom PHP and Nginx config size
  idempotency:
    - mutation accepts operation/idempotency key
    - repeated request returns same operation
    - agent steps check artifact state before creation or deletion

operations_and_locks:
  scopes:
    global_update_lock: release migration only
    hostname_registry_lock: canonical domain and alias reservation across Sites
    site_config_lock: domain list, Nginx and whole-Site operations
    domain_app_lock: provision, deploy, MODX update, PHP change and delete
    database_lock: primary DB replacement and destructive DB action
  ordering:
    - global
    - Site
    - SiteDomain
    - Database
  rules:
    - acquire in fixed order
    - fail fast with current operation metadata
    - persist operation status for process restarts
    - retry only idempotent incomplete steps

modx_management:
  selected_domain_only:
    - use SiteDomain preset, root, PHP, database and credentials
    - construct admin URL from selected canonical domain and managerPath
    - never fall back to Site primary when domainId is present
  update:
    preconditions:
      - MODX preset
      - appStatus RUNNING
      - no deploy/backup/update conflict
      - valid PHP and APP_PRIMARY DB
      - writable root and sufficient disk
    safety:
      - create domain file snapshot
      - create APP_PRIMARY database backup
      - persist restore metadata before mutation
      - redact DB and CMS credentials from logs
    execution:
      - set appStatus UPDATING
      - run updater with selected explicit PHP binary
      - run MODX doctor and setup cleanup
      - probe selected canonical URL
      - persist version only after successful verification
    failure:
      - preserve backup and diagnostics
      - restore automatically when failure occurs after mutation begins
      - set appStatus ERROR only if restoration or final health check fails
      - never affect another domain
  admin_login:
    - selected-domain credentials only
    - ADMIN authorization for secret reveal/change
    - no password in URL, audit payload or application log
    - CSRF-protected one-time server-side login handoff
  version_checks:
    - query every managed MODX domain independently
    - show update badge in selector/Overview
    - no bulk execution action

files:
  root_resolution:
    - SiteDomain.filesRelPath is resolved server-side
    - every operation revalidates containment
    - symlink traversal outside selected root is rejected
  upload_and_extract:
    - preserve existing size and archive safety limits
    - prevent path traversal and special-device extraction
  permissions:
    - normalize only selected domain root
    - same Site system user remains owner

databases:
  selected_domain_behavior:
    - list only Database rows owned by selected SiteDomain
    - create new DB under selected SiteDomain
    - app install receives APP_PRIMARY relation explicitly
  naming:
    - preserve existing global uniqueness rules
    - multi-domain creation reserves all names before provisioning
    - never derive ownership from a database-name prefix after migration
  credentials:
    - preserve encryption and current reveal authorization
    - migration copies relations without decrypting credentials
  deletion:
    - block APP_PRIMARY deletion while managed MODX exists
    - require preset conversion or application deletion first

node_management:
  scope:
    - selected CUSTOM domain root
    - retain existing PM2 process discovery and controls
  constraints:
    - one Linux user means one PM2 namespace per Site
    - process names must be unique across every domain in the Site
    - port allocation remains internal to Node management
    - appPort is not added to generic domain forms
  migration:
    - preserve existing secondary domain filesRelPath and appPort
    - classify existing secondary domain as CUSTOM

logs_and_metrics:
  logs:
    - Nginx logs already map to SiteDomain and remain unchanged
    - PHP log changes from Site anchor to runtimeKey anchor
    - deploy and operation logs gain siteDomainId
    - log APIs require explicit selected domain
  metrics:
    site_level:
      - disk usage
      - Linux-user CPU and memory
      - shared service health
    domain_level:
      - HTTP request/error counts
      - PHP pool process metrics
      - application checks
    honesty_rule: do not label aggregate Linux-user CPU as per-domain CPU
  retention:
    - update logrotate generation for new PHP pool logs
    - preserve historical primary PHP log path or expose archived log explicitly
  scheduler:
    - iterate every main SiteDomain, never aliases
    - store siteDomainId with app-targeted health pings
    - keep one bounded concurrency limit per scheduler run
    - aggregate failures without suppressing healthy sibling domains

backups_restore_and_transfer:
  backup_scope:
    - remain whole-Site
    - include every explicit domain root once
    - include every Site-owned database once
    - record domain-to-root and domain-to-database mapping
  manifest:
    version: increment to v2
    include:
      - Site shared fields
      - all SiteDomain application and routing fields
      - database siteDomainId and purpose
      - preset versions and runtime keys
      - checksums and schema version
    exclude:
      - live Unix sockets
      - copied PHP-FPM/Nginx runtime configs
  restore:
    - v2 restores exact domain/application mapping
    - v1 maps old Site application fields to primary domain
    - v1 secondary domains become CUSTOM
    - regenerate pools and Nginx on target
  server_migration:
    - preflight domain, alias, path, DB, PHP and runtimeKey conflicts
    - recreate runtime configs after files and DBs restore
    - verify every selected-domain URL

duplicate:
  decision: replace ambiguous whole-Site duplicate behavior
  initial_behavior:
    - action operates on currently selected domain/application
    - creates a new Site with that application as its primary domain
    - requires new canonical domain, Site name, directory and database names
  excluded:
    - duplicating every domain of a Site in one click
  reason: hostnames, aliases, database names and external DNS need explicit mapping

security:
  authorization:
    - every domain query is nested under authorized Site ownership
    - ADMIN-only actions remain ADMIN-only
    - no route accepts a foreign domainId under an owned siteId
  secret_handling:
    - copy encrypted values without plaintext conversion during migration
    - redact env, DB, SSH and CMS secrets from logs and migration reports
    - avoid credentials in process argv when supported
  path_handling:
    - central canonical path validator shared across API and agent contracts
    - reject symlink escapes before write/delete/archive operations
  custom_config:
    - retain existing Nginx sanitizer
    - retain PHP pool directive allow/deny validation
    - limit payload size and reject socket/user/listen overrides
  network:
    - generated PHP sockets use restrictive owner/group/mode
    - Node upstream remains loopback-only under current policy
  audit:
    - log actor, Site, SiteDomain, action, result and operationId
    - never log secret values

performance:
  queries:
    - Site list loads aggregate counts with bounded grouped queries
    - Site detail loads lightweight domain summaries once
    - selected domain detail is fetched separately
    - avoid including logs, backups and databases in every Site list row
  indexes:
    - SiteDomain(siteId, position)
    - SiteDomain(siteId, appStatus)
    - SiteDomain(preset)
    - SiteDomain(runtimeKey unique)
    - Database(siteDomainId, purpose)
    - DeployLog(siteDomainId, createdAt)
    - HealthCheckPing(siteDomainId, createdAt) where used
  filesystem:
    - render one Nginx candidate per Site mutation
    - batch PHP service reloads by version during migration
  migration:
    - stream reports instead of retaining unbounded logs
    - group config validation/reloads by service/version

prisma_migration:
  creation:
    command: npx prisma migrate dev --name domain_centric_applications
    rule: never use prisma db push
    implementation:
      - generate migration with create-only workflow when hand-editing is needed
      - use explicit SQLite table-copy SQL for dropped/moved columns
      - preserve IDs, timestamps and encrypted bytes exactly
  schema_steps:
    - create idempotent _meowbox_domain_migration_map staging table
    - add new nullable SiteDomain application columns
    - add nullable Database.siteDomainId and purpose
    - add nullable DeployLog.siteDomainId and related target columns
    - copy primary Site application fields using validated migration-map rows
    - resolve every SiteDomain.filesRelPath to explicit stored relative path
    - assign CUSTOM and safe defaults to existing secondary domains
    - attach existing Site databases using validated migration-map rows
    - assign APP_PRIMARY database from validated migration-map rows
    - attach existing deploy logs to primary SiteDomain
    - verify row counts and invariants
    - rebuild tables with final non-null constraints
    - remove legacy application columns from Site
    - create indexes and partial unique indexes
    - drop _meowbox_domain_migration_map after successful contract checks
  migration_map:
    purpose: >
      Carry filesystem-assisted legacy facts into deterministic SQL without
      guessing and without placing mutable application logic inside migration SQL.
    generation:
      - candidate release scans supported legacy DB and managed MODX config read-only
      - resolve primary SiteDomain, effective roots and APP_PRIMARY database
      - emit one row per Site, SiteDomain and Database with source fingerprints
      - dry-run inserts rows only into cloned SQLite DB
      - apply inserts identical rows after snapshot and quiescence
    validation:
      - map source DB checksum must equal current snapshotted DB checksum
      - every referenced ID must exist and belong to expected Site
      - every supported Site and Database must be covered exactly once
      - duplicate, missing or stale rows abort before Prisma migration
    fresh_install:
      - migration creates an empty staging table
      - empty database has no legacy rows to map
      - final schema is produced normally through prisma migrate deploy
  primary_database_resolution:
    order:
      - use exact persisted relation if introduced by an earlier supported schema
      - use exact managed installer convention when one matching DB exists
      - parse current managed MODX config in preflight and match DB record
      - if only one Site database exists, use it
    failure: abort preflight with Site/domain/database identifiers; never guess
  legacy_mapping:
    primary:
      preset: old Site.type
      filesRelPath: old Site.filesRelPath
      phpVersion: old Site.phpVersion when enabled
      phpPoolCustom: old Site.phpPoolCustom
      appPort: primary SiteDomain.appPort or old Site.appPort
      git_and_env: copy unchanged
      modx_fields: copy unchanged
      runtimeKey: old Site.name
      appStatus: >
        ERROR only for a preserved application/provisioning failure; otherwise
        RUNNING. Global STOPPED remains on Site and does not make appStatus STOPPED.
    secondary:
      preset: CUSTOM
      filesRelPath: coalesce(old SiteDomain.filesRelPath, old Site.filesRelPath)
      appPort: preserve old SiteDomain.appPort
      phpVersion: >
        copy old Site.phpVersion when the current generated Nginx enables PHP
        for that secondary domain; otherwise null
      phpPoolCustom: >
        preserve effective non-resource Site pool settings; split process limits
        according to php_fpm.resource_envelope
      modx_fields: null
      runtimeKey: deterministic from SiteDomain.id
      appStatus: RUNNING unless shared Site is in a blocking error state
      nginx_and_ssl: preserve exactly
  verification:
    - Site row count unchanged
    - SiteDomain row count unchanged
    - Database row count unchanged
    - every Site has exactly one primary domain
    - every SiteDomain has preset, filesRelPath, runtimeKey and appStatus
    - every Database has valid SiteDomain in same Site
    - every MODX domain has APP_PRIMARY DB and PHP version
    - PRAGMA integrity_check returns ok
    - PRAGMA foreign_key_check returns zero rows

prisma_history_baseline:
  problem: current updater uses db push on deployments without reliable migration history
  required_fix:
    - stop using db push in update.sh
    - detect supported legacy schema by exact table/column/index fingerprint
    - reject unknown drift before mutation
    - baseline only when fingerprint matches an explicitly supported release schema
    - record historical migrations as applied without executing them
    - execute new migration through prisma migrate deploy
  safeguards:
    - baseline tool is idempotent
    - existing valid _prisma_migrations is never rewritten
    - failed/partial Prisma migration state blocks update
    - baseline decision is included in dry-run report

system_migration:
  required_because:
    - PHP-FPM pool templates and ownership change
    - PHP logrotate paths change
    - Nginx PHP socket payload changes
  artifact_changes:
    - create per-domain pool files for PHP-enabled domains
    - preserve migrated primary compatibility key
    - create per-domain temp/session/log directories where required
    - render each domain 20-php.conf against its own socket
    - update logrotate config
    - remove obsolete Site-only pool only after cutover succeeds
  implementation:
    - one idempotent system migration
    - explicit plan/preflight function with zero writes
    - prepare, validate, commit and cleanup checkpoints
    - checkpoint state persisted under state/data/migrations
    - every write uses atomic rename and preserves mode/owner
  validation:
    - validate staged PHP-FPM configurations for all affected versions
    - validate complete staged Nginx config
    - verify runtime socket path lengths
    - verify required PHP services and binaries exist
    - verify no custom config references a disappearing managed artifact
  regeneration_scope:
    - every existing Site once during migration
    - only affected Site during later domain changes

dry_run:
  automatic: always runs before apply in make update
  standalone: expose update dry-run command for operators
  production_mutation: forbidden
  steps:
    - download and verify candidate release
    - run candidate preflight code from staging release
    - acquire read lock/check no conflicting update
    - record hashes of live SQLite DB and managed config trees
    - create consistent SQLite clone using SQLite backup API
    - fingerprint legacy schema and simulate Prisma baseline on clone
    - run prisma migrate deploy against clone
    - execute all data verification against clone
    - render PHP-FPM, Nginx and logrotate candidates into temp tree
    - validate candidate PHP-FPM configs
    - validate candidate Nginx config without replacing live files
    - calculate exact create/change/delete artifact manifest
    - check disk, permissions, packages, services and socket path limits
    - check for active provision/deploy/MODX update/backup operations
    - compare live hashes to prove dry-run made no production changes
    - write redacted machine-readable and human-readable report
  result:
    pass: update may enter maintenance and apply
    fail: update exits before stopping services or changing DB/config

release_update_transaction:
  constraint: true atomicity across SQLite and OS files is impossible
  user_visible_behavior: one command either completes new release or restores old release
  phases:
    U01_stage:
      - download release and checksum
      - extract candidate
      - validate package contains schema, Prisma migration and system migration
    U02_dry_run:
      - execute full dry_run contract
    U03_snapshot:
      - create consistent SQLite backup
      - snapshot Nginx managed tree with owners, modes and symlink targets
      - snapshot PHP-FPM managed pools and logrotate files with metadata
      - record current release symlink and process state
    U04_quiesce:
      - reject new panel mutations
      - wait bounded time for active operations
      - acquire one OS flock shared by updater, migration runner and startup repair
      - stop API schedulers/workers and agent mutation endpoint
      - disable/gate API startup artifact repair until migration commit
      - keep hosted sites serving through current Nginx/PHP config
      - serve panel maintenance response
    U05_database:
      - baseline supported legacy DB if required
      - run prisma migrate deploy
      - run integrity, foreign-key, count and invariant checks
    U06_prepare_runtime:
      - write new pool/config candidates
      - validate PHP-FPM and Nginx
      - start/reload new PHP pools and verify sockets
    U07_switch:
      - atomically replace managed runtime configs
      - reload affected PHP-FPM services by version
      - reload Nginx
      - atomically switch current release symlink
      - restart API, Web and agent with new release
    U08_verify:
      - API health
      - Web health and current Nuxt build metadata
      - agent health
      - Nginx config
      - PHP sockets
      - selected HTTP probes for every SiteDomain
      - DB integrity and representative API reads
    U09_commit:
      - mark rollback boundary after every final verification passes
      - re-enable API/agent writes
      - write success sentinel only now
      - remove obsolete Site-only pool files as idempotent post-commit cleanup
      - reload affected PHP services and recheck after cleanup
      - leave snapshot under normal retention policy
      - publish redacted migration report
  rollback_trigger:
    - any failure from quiesce through verification
  rollback:
    - stop candidate API/Web/agent
    - restore previous release symlink
    - restore SQLite DB backup including WAL-safe state
    - restore Nginx, PHP-FPM and logrotate snapshots
    - reload old PHP-FPM services
    - validate and reload old Nginx
    - start old API/Web/agent
    - run old release health checks
    - preserve candidate logs and failure report
  after_commit_failure:
    - never restore the old DB automatically after writes reopen
    - keep new release serving when core health remains valid
    - run idempotent forward repair for cleanup/reporting failures
    - require explicit maintenance and a new snapshot for any later rollback
  success_sentinel:
    rule: never write before PM2/systemd health and application probes pass
  availability:
    - panel writes are unavailable during maintenance
    - hosted static traffic should continue through current Nginx
    - Nginx reload is graceful
    - PHP-FPM pool transition may cause a brief PHP request interruption
    - zero downtime is not promised for this schema/runtime cutover

migration_mutation_boundary:
  panel_database:
    mutation: schema and ownership data are changed
    rollback: consistent SQLite snapshot
  managed_runtime_config:
    mutation: Nginx, PHP-FPM and logrotate files are changed
    rollback: metadata-preserving config snapshot
  application_files:
    mutation: forbidden during release migration
    consequence: no application-root restore is needed for release rollback
  application_databases:
    mutation: forbidden during release migration
    consequence: no customer DB restore is needed for release rollback
  ssl_state:
    mutation: certificates are not reissued or deleted by this migration

migration_preflight_blockers:
  - unsupported or drifted SQLite schema fingerprint
  - failed or partial prior Prisma migration
  - failed or partial prior system migration
  - SQLite integrity or foreign-key error
  - Site without exactly one primary domain
  - canonical domain/alias collision
  - invalid or escaping filesRelPath
  - unresolved managed MODX primary database
  - missing supported PHP binary or php-fpm service
  - PHP runtime key or socket collision
  - socket path over platform limit
  - invalid existing PHP pool custom directives
  - invalid current or candidate Nginx config
  - insufficient free disk for DB/config snapshots and staging
  - replacement PHP pool worker/memory budget exceeds safe host headroom
  - active provisioning, deploy, MODX update, restore or destructive backup job
  - custom config referencing an artifact that migration cannot preserve safely

compatibility_and_edge_cases:
  E01:
    case: existing secondary domain inherits primary filesRelPath
    action: >
      preserve explicit resolved path, assign CUSTOM, preserve its effective
      current PHP capability, and report shared root
  E02:
    case: existing secondary domain has appPort
    action: preserve value and existing Nginx behavior; do not expose generic field
  E03:
    case: primary MODX Site has several databases
    action: resolve APP_PRIMARY deterministically or block update
  E04:
    case: Site has no database but claims MODX preset
    action: block migration with exact remediation data
  E05:
    case: Site is STOPPED
    action: migrate data/config but preserve global stopped state
  E06:
    case: Site or app is ERROR
    action: preserve error state and diagnostics; do not invent RUNNING
  E07:
    case: duplicate existing domain roots
    action: preserve; block destructive file deletion; reject new duplicate
  E08:
    case: aliases contain another canonical domain
    action: preflight block because routing is ambiguous
  E09:
    case: domain rename after migration
    action: preserve app artifacts/runtime key; regenerate routing/SSL only
  E10:
    case: primary domain changes
    action: switch primary flags only; no app/data movement
  E11:
    case: two domains use different PHP versions
    action: separate pools, shared service per version, explicit binary per operation
  E12:
    case: two domains use same PHP version
    action: separate pools/sockets under same phpX.Y-fpm service
  E13:
    case: custom Nginx domain proxies Node
    action: preserve config and internal appPort behavior
  E14:
    case: old backup or transfer manifest
    action: v1 compatibility mapper creates primary app and CUSTOM secondaries
  E15:
    case: operation process dies mid-provision
    action: resume from persisted idempotent step state
  E16:
    case: migration dies after DB change but before runtime switch
    action: update rollback restores DB and runtime snapshot, then old release
  E17:
    case: SSL issuance fails for one new domain
    action: keep app HTTP-capable and report SSL failure separately
  E18:
    case: selected domain disappears while Web UI is open
    action: 404 domain API, refresh summaries, fall back to primary
  E19:
    case: stale browser calls old Site-level endpoint
    action: explicit error; never mutate primary implicitly
  E20:
    case: manual files exist in new MODX target directory
    action: reject install before mutation
  E21:
    case: one old Site pool served several PHP-enabled domains
    action: >
      create one pool per domain while preserving the old aggregate worker
      ceiling; never multiply worst-case memory silently

execution_task_graph:
  T001_contract_freeze:
    depends_on: []
    work:
      - approve fixed decisions D01-D14 as implementation contract
      - enumerate every current Site application field and every reader/writer
      - enumerate every SiteDomain routing field and preserve its semantics
      - document supported source release/schema fingerprints
    done_when:
      - no unclassified Site application field remains
      - no route or background job lacks a target ownership decision

  T002_upgrade_fixtures:
    depends_on: [T001_contract_freeze]
    work:
      - produce sanitized SQLite/config fixtures from supported releases
      - include single-domain MODX 2, MODX 3 and CUSTOM
      - include multi-domain, appPort, shared-root, multiple-DB and error states
      - include valid and absent Prisma migration histories
    done_when:
      - fixtures contain no secrets or customer content
      - every legacy_mapping branch has a fixture

  T003_schema_design:
    depends_on: [T001_contract_freeze]
    work:
      - update Prisma models and enums
      - define raw SQLite partial indexes
      - define Domain/Database/DeployLog relations and delete policies
      - generate typed shared API models
    done_when:
      - schema expresses all final required fields
      - no legacy Site application field exists in final model
      - Prisma validate/generate passes

  T004_legacy_mapper:
    depends_on: [T002_upgrade_fixtures, T003_schema_design]
    work:
      - implement read-only schema fingerprinting
      - resolve effective roots and runtime keys
      - resolve APP_PRIMARY database deterministically
      - emit migration-map rows and blockers
      - redact report values
    done_when:
      - identical input produces byte-identical mapping
      - ambiguous input fails before mutation

  T005_prisma_baseline:
    depends_on: [T002_upgrade_fixtures, T003_schema_design]
    work:
      - detect trustworthy existing Prisma history
      - baseline exact supported db-push schemas
      - reject drift and partial history
      - remove db push from install/update paths
    done_when:
      - migrate deploy works on fresh, baselined and already-tracked fixtures
      - unknown schema never receives an automatic baseline

  T006_prisma_migration:
    depends_on: [T004_legacy_mapper, T005_prisma_baseline]
    work:
      - generate migration through prisma migrate dev
      - hand-review SQLite table-copy SQL
      - consume and validate migration-map staging rows
      - copy application fields and relations
      - enforce final non-null/unique constraints
      - drop legacy fields and staging table
    done_when:
      - all fixtures reach one identical final schema
      - row counts, integrity and foreign keys pass
      - second migrate deploy is a no-op

  T007_operation_framework:
    depends_on: [T003_schema_design]
    work:
      - persist parent and domain child operations
      - implement Site and SiteDomain locks
      - add idempotency keys and resumable step state
      - add redacted progress/error transport to Web UI
    done_when:
      - process restart resumes or safely fails each operation
      - conflicting mutations cannot run concurrently

  T008_domain_context:
    depends_on: [T003_schema_design]
    work:
      - implement requireOwnedSiteDomain
      - implement canonical hostname and path validators
      - implement selected-domain application context mapper
      - remove implicit primary fallback from reusable app services
    done_when:
      - every app service requires explicit SiteDomain context
      - IDOR and path traversal tests pass

  T009_php_pool_identity:
    depends_on: [T003_schema_design, T008_domain_context]
    work:
      - make pool renderer accept SiteDomain runtime context
      - preserve migrated primary pool compatibility
      - generate new-domain pool/socket/log artifacts and validated temp/session paths
      - validate socket limits and directive restrictions
      - preserve aggregate legacy worker budget when one pool becomes several
    done_when:
      - mixed PHP versions work under shared per-version services
      - domain rename and make-primary do not change pool identity
      - migration does not silently multiply worst-case PHP worker memory

  T010_nginx_domain_runtime:
    depends_on: [T008_domain_context, T009_php_pool_identity]
    work:
      - move PHP payload from Site to each rendered SiteDomain
      - retain current server-block and chunk paths
      - preserve exact custom chunks and appPort behavior
      - stage, validate, atomically switch and restore configs
    done_when:
      - mixed PHP/static/proxy golden tests pass
      - failed validation or probe restores active config

  T011_domain_installer:
    depends_on: [T007_operation_framework, T008_domain_context, T009_php_pool_identity, T010_nginx_domain_runtime]
    work:
      - accept explicit domain preset/runtime/DB context
      - provision multiple application rows for new Site
      - provision one additional domain for existing Site
      - track created artifacts for rollback
      - keep SSL failure separate from application failure
    done_when:
      - one Site can provision three mixed applications
      - failure never removes pre-existing content or another app

  T012_modx_domain_lifecycle:
    depends_on: [T007_operation_framework, T008_domain_context, T011_domain_installer]
    work:
      - scope install, update, doctor, cleanup and permissions to domain
      - scope credentials and admin login to domain
      - add file/DB safety snapshot before MODX update
      - verify and restore selected app only
    done_when:
      - two MODX apps update and authenticate independently
      - forced failure restores selected app and leaves peer unchanged

  T013_database_domain_ownership:
    depends_on: [T006_prisma_migration, T008_domain_context]
    work:
      - filter CRUD by selected domain
      - enforce APP_PRIMARY rules
      - update installer, updater and backup consumers
      - block destructive primary DB deletion
    done_when:
      - no app operation discovers DB by Site/name guess
      - cross-domain DB access is rejected

  T014_domain_crud:
    depends_on: [T007_operation_framework, T008_domain_context, T010_nginx_domain_runtime, T013_database_domain_ownership]
    work:
      - implement nested create/edit/retry/delete/make-primary APIs
      - enforce last-domain, primary and shared-root guards
      - preserve app identity during rename/primary switch
      - make deletion cleanup explicit and auditable
    done_when:
      - all domain_management rules pass integration tests

  T015_domain_deploy_node:
    depends_on: [T007_operation_framework, T008_domain_context]
    work:
      - move deploy status/logs/git/env to SiteDomain
      - scope Node.js process discovery to selected root
      - enforce PM2 name uniqueness across shared Site user
      - keep port allocation internal
    done_when:
      - deploy/Node actions affect selected CUSTOM domain only
      - generic APIs and forms never expose appPort

  T016_domain_files_logs_metrics:
    depends_on: [T008_domain_context, T009_php_pool_identity]
    work:
      - scope file root to selected domain
      - map Nginx and PHP logs to selected domain
      - add domain IDs to deploy/audit/health records
      - separate honest domain metrics from aggregate Site metrics
      - update logrotate
    done_when:
      - selection changes files/logs/metrics deterministically
      - aggregate CPU is never mislabeled as domain CPU

  T017_site_aggregates:
    depends_on: [T003_schema_design, T013_database_domain_ownership]
    work:
      - rewrite Site list/detail projections
      - derive preset counts and aggregate app status efficiently
      - keep global Site lifecycle separate from app lifecycle
      - remove singular Site type/version/port projections
    done_when:
      - list queries are bounded and indexed
      - no N+1 domain/application query remains

  T018_web_domain_context:
    depends_on: [T008_domain_context, T017_site_aggregates]
    work:
      - implement header domain selector
      - persist explicit domainId in URL
      - implement primary fallback and conditional tab behavior
      - propagate domainId through all domain-scoped API calls
    done_when:
      - aliases are absent from selector
      - refresh/deep-link/stale-selection E2E tests pass

  T019_web_creation:
    depends_on: [T011_domain_installer, T014_domain_crud]
    work:
      - build reusable preset form
      - support repeatable domain rows in create Site wizard
      - reuse same form for add Domain
      - provide per-domain review and operation results
    done_when:
      - create/add forms share validation and preset logic
      - no directory hierarchy or appPort is invented

  T020_web_scoped_tabs:
    depends_on: [T012_modx_domain_lifecycle, T015_domain_deploy_node, T016_domain_files_logs_metrics, T018_web_domain_context]
    work:
      - scope Overview, SSL, Nginx, PHP, DB, Files, Node, Logs, MODX, Deploy
      - preserve Site-scoped Backups, Cron, Services, SSH and Danger
      - replace duplicate action with selected-app-to-new-Site flow
      - remove stale Site-level app controls
    done_when:
      - every tab clearly follows domain or Site scope
      - desktop/mobile E2E has no stale context or overlapping controls

  T021_backup_manifest_v2:
    depends_on: [T006_prisma_migration, T013_database_domain_ownership]
    work:
      - serialize full domain app mapping
      - deduplicate shared roots
      - implement v1 compatibility mapping
      - regenerate runtime configs after restore
    done_when:
      - v1 and v2 restore tests pass
      - restored Site preserves app/domain/DB ownership

  T022_transfer_import:
    depends_on: [T021_backup_manifest_v2, T011_domain_installer]
    work:
      - update server transfer snapshot
      - update hostpanel import output to explicit existing presets
      - preflight target conflicts for every domain
      - remove any general adoption/unmanaged path from this feature
    done_when:
      - clean VPS transfer rebuilds pools/Nginx and probes every domain
      - no imported app has implicit or unmanaged type

  T023_system_migration:
    depends_on: [T006_prisma_migration, T009_php_pool_identity, T010_nginx_domain_runtime, T016_domain_files_logs_metrics]
    work:
      - implement idempotent per-domain pool/Nginx/logrotate regeneration
      - preserve primary compatibility artifacts
      - snapshot, validate, switch and clean obsolete pools
      - persist checkpoints and redacted report
    done_when:
      - second run is no-op
      - interruption at each checkpoint resumes or restores safely

  T024_real_dry_run:
    depends_on: [T004_legacy_mapper, T005_prisma_baseline, T006_prisma_migration, T023_system_migration]
    work:
      - clone SQLite consistently
      - run identical baseline/map/migrate path on clone
      - render and validate all runtime configs in staging
      - prove live DB/config hashes unchanged
      - expose automatic and standalone report
    done_when:
      - supported fixtures pass without live changes
      - every blocker fails before maintenance mode

  T025_update_transaction:
    depends_on: [T024_real_dry_run]
    work:
      - stage release before mutation
      - snapshot DB/config/current release
      - quiesce panel mutation processes
      - apply DB and system migrations
      - switch/restart/verify
      - restore all layers on failure
      - move success sentinel after final health checks
    done_when:
      - forced failure at every mutating phase restores healthy old release
      - successful update leaves no old Site-only source of truth

  T026_stale_contract_removal:
    depends_on: [T014_domain_crud, T020_web_scoped_tabs, T022_transfer_import]
    work:
      - remove old Site-level app routes and DTO fields
      - remove old shared API projections and Web controls
      - remove old Site-level agent event payloads
      - scan source for every removed schema field
    done_when:
      - compiler and structural search show no forbidden legacy ownership
      - stale clients receive explicit failure, never primary fallback

  T027_full_rehearsal:
    depends_on: [T021_backup_manifest_v2, T022_transfer_import, T025_update_transaction, T026_stale_contract_removal]
    work:
      - run unit, integration, agent, Web and migration suites
      - upgrade all sanitized production fixtures
      - perform failure injection and rollback matrix
      - test clean VPS installation
      - test backup/restore and VPS transfer
    done_when:
      - quality_gates and acceptance_criteria all pass
      - dry-run/apply reports are reviewed

  T028_release:
    depends_on: [T027_full_rehearsal]
    work:
      - run make snapshot before local dangerous rehearsal if applicable
      - bump VERSION
      - commit under operator identity
      - tag and publish release artifact/checksums
      - verify release workflow and downloadable package
      - run post-release update rehearsal from published artifact
    done_when:
      - published artifact upgrades old VPS and installs clean VPS correctly
      - no implementation work or migration gap remains

parallelization:
  after_T003:
    - T007_operation_framework
    - T008_domain_context
    - T005_prisma_baseline
  after_runtime_contract:
    - API domain lifecycle work
    - backup manifest work
    - Web aggregate/domain-state shell
  serialized:
    - final Prisma migration review
    - system migration
    - updater transaction
    - release rehearsal and release

code_impact_map:
  schema_and_migrations:
    modify:
      - api/prisma/schema.prisma
      - migrations/runner.ts
      - migrations/system/_types.ts when plan/journal context changes
    add:
      - api/prisma/migrations/<domain-centric-id>/migration.sql
      - migrations/system/<domain-runtime-id>.ts
      - migration mapper, fingerprint and invariant-check modules
    never_modify:
      - already-applied Prisma migration SQL
      - already-applied system migration files
  release_tooling:
    modify:
      - tools/update.sh
      - tools/snapshot.sh
      - tools/rollback.sh
      - tools/healthcheck.sh
      - Makefile
    verify:
      - release workflow packages Prisma and compiled system migrations
      - checksums cover every migration artifact
  shared_contracts:
    modify:
      - shared/src/entities.ts
      - shared/src/api.ts
      - shared/src/enums.ts
      - shared/src/site-artifacts.ts
      - shared/src/node-app.ts where domain ownership is represented
  api_site_core:
    modify:
      - api/src/sites/sites.dto.ts
      - api/src/sites/sites.service.ts
      - api/src/sites/sites.controller.ts
      - api/src/sites/site-domains.dto.ts
      - api/src/sites/site-domains.helper.ts
      - api/src/sites/site-domains.service.ts
      - api/src/sites/site-domains.controller.ts
      - api/src/sites/sites-nginx.service.ts
    add:
      - owned SiteDomain context guard/helper
      - durable domain operation service
      - migration map and invariant services
  api_consumers:
    inspect_and_migrate:
      - deploy service and controller
      - MODX update/doctor/credential routes and services
      - PHP pool routes and services
      - files routes and services
      - database routes and services
      - logs routes and services
      - scheduler and health checks
      - Site Node.js service
      - metrics collectors and projections
      - backup, restore and duplicate services
      - Meowbox migration service
      - HostPanel migration plan/run services
      - audit interceptor domain identity extraction
      - startup artifact-repair hooks
  agent:
    modify:
      - agent/src/nginx/templates.ts
      - agent/src/nginx/nginx.manager.ts
      - agent/src/php/phpfpm.manager.ts
      - agent/src/agent.service.ts
      - agent/src/system/site-metrics.collector.ts
      - agent deploy executor
      - agent Node.js manager
      - Site installer and permissions modules
      - MODX installer/updater/doctor modules
      - HostPanel migration item runner and contracts
  web:
    modify:
      - web/pages/sites/create.vue
      - web/pages/sites/index.vue
      - web/pages/sites/[id].vue
      - web/components/SiteDomainsTab.vue
      - Site Overview/Nginx/PHP/SSL/Database/Files/Logs/Node/MODX/Deploy tabs
      - HostPanel migration UI where destination ownership is serialized
    add:
      - reusable domain preset form
      - Site header domain selector
      - selected-domain URL state/composable
      - per-domain operation progress component
  documentation:
    update:
      - backup/restore format
      - server migration format
      - Site/domain ownership model
      - PHP-FPM pool topology
      - operator update/dry-run/rollback runbook

implementation_workstreams:
  W01_schema:
    deliverables:
      - final Prisma schema
      - generated and reviewed migration SQL
      - schema fingerprint/baseline tool
      - migration invariant checker
  W02_domain_context:
    deliverables:
      - shared requireOwnedSiteDomain guard
      - normalized application context mapper
      - shared path/runtime validation
      - operation locks
  W03_agent_runtime:
    deliverables:
      - per-domain PHP pool generation
      - per-domain logs/temp/session paths
      - domain-aware installer/updater/deployer
      - atomic Nginx and PHP config transitions
  W04_api:
    deliverables:
      - nested create Site domains request
      - add/retry/edit/delete/make-primary flows
      - domain-scoped MODX/PHP/files/logs/deploy/DB/Node routes
      - aggregate Site list/detail responses
  W05_web:
    deliverables:
      - repeatable create wizard rows
      - unified add-domain/preset form
      - header domain selector and URL state
      - scoped tabs/actions
      - aggregate Site list
  W06_backup_transfer:
    deliverables:
      - v2 backup/transfer manifest
      - v1 compatibility mapper
      - domain-aware restore and target regeneration
  W07_release:
    deliverables:
      - real clone-based dry-run
      - maintenance/quiesce phase
      - reversible config snapshot
      - corrected success sentinel and rollback
      - removal of db push
  W08_observability:
    deliverables:
      - per-domain logs and audit IDs
      - migration report
      - operation status UI

implementation_order:
  - W01 schema and migration contract
  - W02 domain context, invariants and locks
  - W03 agent runtime and config validation
  - W04 API migration
  - W05 Web UI migration
  - W06 backup/restore/transfer compatibility
  - W07 updater, dry-run and rollback
  - W08 observability and final hardening
  - full rehearsal and one release

test_plan:
  unit:
    schema_and_mapping:
      - primary MODX_REVO mapping
      - primary MODX_3 mapping
      - primary CUSTOM mapping
      - secondary CUSTOM mapping
      - inherited and explicit filesRelPath
      - legacy appPort preservation
      - multiple DB primary resolution
      - encrypted field byte preservation
    validation:
      - hostname and alias normalization/conflicts
      - relative path containment and symlink escapes
      - runtime key determinism and socket length
      - preset/PHP/DB contracts
      - domain ownership guard
    state:
      - application transitions
      - Site aggregate status
      - operation lock ordering
  migration_fixtures:
    - pristine current schema
    - current schema with valid Prisma history
    - current schema without Prisma history
    - old supported release snapshots
    - Site with one domain
    - Site with several secondary domains
    - secondary domains sharing root
    - different per-domain Nginx/SSL settings
    - Site with multiple databases
    - stopped and error Sites
    - malformed unsupported drift must fail before mutation
  agent:
    - two domains on same PHP version create distinct pools/sockets
    - two domains on different versions use correct services
    - legacy one-pool-to-many split preserves aggregate worker ceiling
    - insufficient FPM headroom blocks before service changes
    - pool update rollback
    - PHP version switch rollback
    - explicit PHP binary for install/update
    - Nginx per-domain PHP/static/proxy golden renders
    - custom Nginx bytes preserved
    - nginx -t failure restores old config
  api_integration:
    - create Site with one domain
    - create Site with three mixed presets
    - add MODX and CUSTOM domains
    - retry failed domain provisioning
    - domain rename
    - make-primary
    - delete guards and shared-root protection
    - foreign domainId authorization rejection
    - concurrent provision/update/delete rejection
    - database ownership and APP_PRIMARY guards
  modx:
    - two MODX applications inside one Site
    - independent versions and PHP versions
    - update first without touching second
    - update rollback from file and DB failure
    - admin password and auto-login per selected domain
    - doctor and setup cleanup per selected root
  backup_and_transfer:
    - whole-Site backup with multiple roots and DBs
    - deduplicate shared legacy root
    - v2 restore
    - v1 restore mapping
    - transfer to clean VPS and regenerate pools/Nginx
  web_e2e:
    - selector visible only for multiple main domains
    - aliases absent
    - query-param deep links
    - invalid selection fallback
    - MODX/PHP tabs conditional
    - Files/Logs/DB content changes with selector
    - destructive dialog names selected domain/path
    - create three-domain wizard validation
    - desktop and mobile layout without overlap
  release_rehearsal:
    - dry-run leaves DB/config hashes unchanged
    - full upgrade on cloned production snapshots
    - forced failure after each update phase
    - old release fully restored after each forced failure
    - interrupted update resumes or rolls back idempotently
    - second update run is a no-op
    - new clean VPS installation supports same model

quality_gates:
  code:
    - formatting, lint and type checks pass
    - API, agent and Web builds pass
    - no Site-level application field references remain
    - no ambiguous primary-domain fallback in domain actions
  migration:
    - Prisma migration generated through migrate dev
    - no db push in install/update paths
    - dry-run against every supported fixture
    - DB row-count, integrity and foreign-key checks pass
    - system migration is idempotent
  runtime:
    - php-fpm validation passes for every supported version
    - nginx -t passes
    - every expected socket exists
    - all canonical domain HTTP probes return expected class
  security:
    - path traversal suite passes
    - cross-Site domain authorization suite passes
    - migration and operation logs contain no secrets
  release:
    - package contains migration SQL and compiled system migration
    - rollback rehearsal passes
    - success sentinel occurs only after final health checks

acceptance_criteria:
  A01:
    given: new Site wizard
    when: operator adds three domain rows with mixed presets
    then: one Site and three independently managed domain applications are created
  A02:
    given: existing Site
    when: operator adds another domain with MODX preset and explicit directory
    then: MODX, DB, PHP pool, Nginx and SSL belong to that domain
  A03:
    given: Site with two MODX domains
    when: one domain is selected
    then: update, doctor, credentials and admin login affect only that MODX
  A04:
    given: two PHP domains on same version
    then: they use separate pools/sockets under one phpX.Y-fpm service
  A05:
    given: two PHP domains on different versions
    then: each uses its configured version without changing the other
  A06:
    given: Site detail header
    when: domain selection changes
    then: selected-domain tabs and actions change without a second app selector
  A07:
    given: alias
    then: it routes to its parent domain app and is absent from selector
  A08:
    given: existing secondary domain during upgrade
    then: it becomes CUSTOM with exact current path, appPort, Nginx and SSL state
  A09:
    given: current primary application during upgrade
    then: preset, path, PHP, DB, credentials and MODX version are preserved
  A10:
    given: unsupported or ambiguous legacy data
    then: automatic dry-run blocks update before production mutation
  A11:
    given: failure after schema migration begins
    then: DB, runtime configs and old release are restored and old health passes
  A12:
    given: clean VPS installation of release
    then: multi-domain application creation works without legacy migration steps
  A13:
    given: MODX update failure
    then: selected app files and primary DB restore without touching other domains
  A14:
    given: domain delete with shared root
    then: file deletion is refused
  A15:
    given: stale client without domainId
    then: API never silently targets primary application

release_definition_of_done:
  - all fixed decisions D01-D14 implemented
  - all migration blockers produce actionable redacted diagnostics
  - all acceptance criteria A01-A15 pass
  - migration rehearsed against supported real-world DB/config snapshots
  - rollback rehearsed after forced failure at every mutating phase
  - clean installation and in-place update produce same final schema/runtime model
  - documentation describes domain selector, per-domain presets and backup semantics
  - VERSION bumped before commit/tag
  - release built, checksums published and update workflow verified
